# Byte-exact checkouts.
#
# The credibility of this repository rests on frozen evidence that is verified
# by SHA-256 (see CODE/verify_frozen_evidence.py and
# EVALS/FROZEN_EVIDENCE_MANIFEST.json).  With the default core.autocrlf=true,
# Git rewrites line endings on checkout, so a clone on Windows would receive
# different bytes from the author's working tree and the verification would
# fail for reasons that have nothing to do with the experiments.
#
# Therefore: store every file exactly as it is on disk and never convert line
# endings, in either direction.  "git clone" then reproduces the working tree
# byte for byte, on any platform.
* -text
